sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/aristotle-ga02-07> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Birds and scaly reptiles lay a complete egg because they are hot, but only an egg rather than live young because they are dry; the reproductive mode follows from an animal's heat and moisture.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Heat and dryness explain why birds and reptiles lay complete eggs";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Aristotle, On the Generation of Animals (De Generatione Animalium), Book II; translated by Arthur Platt, The Works of Aristotle Translated into English, ed. J. A. Smith and W. D. Ross, Oxford: Clarendon Press, vol. V (1912). Scope: Birds and scaly reptiles, within his heat-and-moisture account of viviparity and oviparity"
}
